From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] config: build the NBD virtual-media Redfish routes
Upstream-Status: Pending

bmcweb ships a complete Redfish VirtualMedia client in
redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp, but upstream compiles it out
unconditionally: the meson option was commented out of meson.options and the
constant hardcoded to false, on the grounds that no daemon implementing
xyz.openbmc_project.VirtualMedia was ever upstreamed.

One does exist -- Intel-BMC/virtual-media -- and this layer packages it, so
the routes have a backend to talk to. Flip the constant rather than
resurrecting the meson option, so there is exactly one place to look and no
build configuration that can silently disagree with the recipe.

Without this, /redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/VirtualMedia returns 404 and the
Manager resource omits the VirtualMedia link entirely, which reads like the
daemon is missing rather than like the route was compiled out.

--- a/config/meson.build
+++ b/config/meson.build
@@ -108,8 +108,8 @@
 loglvlopt = loglvlopt.to_upper()
 string_options_string += 'constexpr std::string_view  BMCWEB_LOGGING_LEVEL' + ' = "' + loglvlopt + '";\n'
 
-# NBD proxy is disabled due to lack of maintenance.  See meson_options.txt
-feature_options_string += 'constexpr const bool BMCWEB_VM_NBDPROXY = false;\n'
+# Re-enabled for this board: Intel-BMC/virtual-media provides the backend.
+feature_options_string += 'constexpr const bool BMCWEB_VM_NBDPROXY = true;\n'
 
 conf_data.set(
     'BMCWEB_OPTIONS',
